-- title:
--   Row-10 reduced square polynomial coefficients
-- statement:
--   These are explicit finite coefficient data for the degree-10 inverse cubic of a fifth power of $z^3-z-\beta$. The algebraic parameter used in the later proofs satisfies $\alpha^3=1001/20-66\alpha+21\alpha^2$. The bundle defines the explicit polynomial $S_\alpha(t)$ of degree at most 62, with rational quadratic expressions in $\alpha$ as coefficients. It is the reduced square of the degree-at-most-31 Newton approximant: the identity $P_\alpha(t)^2=S_\alpha(t)$ under the stated cubic relation is proved separately. This coefficient table makes the residual and inverse-derivative certificates verifiable in smaller arithmetic stages.
-- source:
--   https://gist.github.com/Amal-David/adce933460b7501cb123f483f62775eb/f5a76eda649f3e995a8ec6b98387b23b64c6debb#file-fifth-md; H5_COMPLETE_CHAIN.md, Sections 1–4; lower/H5_LOWER_MIDDLE_COMPLETION.md and upper/H5_UPPER_BRIDGE.md in the archived research checkpoint. The finite Newton coefficient arrays are auxiliary exact certificates constructed for the accompanying Lean formalization, and are specified in full by this definition submission.

